# REPORTING

Every module that holds tabular or summary data must support export through the shared stack.

## Formats

| Format | Rule |
|---|---|
| CSV | Always via `downloadCsv` / `ExportMenu` |
| Excel | SpreadsheetML `.xls` via `downloadExcelFile` (multi-sheet when useful) |
| PDF | Printable HTML → browser **Print → Save as PDF** (no fake PDF claims) |
| Print | `openPrintableReport` / print CSS |
| Shareable links | Token snapshot at `/share/report/:token` — label device/expiry limits honestly |
| Scheduled | Local cadence (`schedule.js`) while app is open; do not claim email until server job exists |

## Architecture

- Shared API: `src/lib/export/*`
- UI: `ExportMenu` on list/report pages
- Specs: `moduleSpecs.js` (Jobs, Customers, Invoices, Finances, Analytics, Reports pack)
- Driver Hub may keep domain builders but should call shared download helpers

## Honesty

- Marketplace / copy must not advertise formats that are not wired  
- Share links are device-local until a signed cloud share API ships  
- Schedules toast/download in-app — not silent email  

## Definition of done

Incomplete if a History/Reports/Analytics list page has no ExportMenu, if PDF is claimed without a print path, or if schedule implies email delivery that does not exist.
